{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00195",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.11,
      "end_seconds": 3.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Hello. Right, let's get started."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.64,
      "end_seconds": 6.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.9,
      "end_seconds": 8.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Okay. Start wherever you like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.45,
      "end_seconds": 11.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "I've been dealing with wheezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.12,
      "end_seconds": 14.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.65,
      "end_seconds": 17.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "It's been three days, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.33,
      "end_seconds": 28.1,
      "duration_seconds": 7.77,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.61,
      "end_seconds": 35.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "About a five out of ten. It just comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.79,
      "end_seconds": 39.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Have you been using your blue inhaler more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.67,
      "end_seconds": 42.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Yes, since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.83,
      "end_seconds": 44.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "How much is it bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.19,
      "end_seconds": 48.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "A three out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.35,
      "end_seconds": 53.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.27,
      "end_seconds": 54.97,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.59,
      "end_seconds": 69.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Have you had any fever or leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.45,
      "end_seconds": 73.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.29,
      "end_seconds": 77.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.68,
      "end_seconds": 90.73,
      "duration_seconds": 12.05,
      "text": "Not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.55,
      "end_seconds": 98.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.1,
      "end_seconds": 101.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.55,
      "end_seconds": 117.37,
      "duration_seconds": 14.82,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.26,
      "end_seconds": 120.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.85,
      "end_seconds": 122.81,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.93,
      "end_seconds": 125.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "No, nothing regular."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.35,
      "end_seconds": 130.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.0,
      "end_seconds": 133.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.21,
      "end_seconds": 135.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.27,
      "end_seconds": 137.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.5,
      "end_seconds": 143.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Sorry about the noise outside, the building work never stops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.37,
      "end_seconds": 146.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "I hadn't even noticed, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.19,
      "end_seconds": 153.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.48,
      "end_seconds": 156.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "No, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.82,
      "end_seconds": 160.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.23,
      "end_seconds": 178.0,
      "duration_seconds": 15.77,
      "text": "Not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.43,
      "end_seconds": 195.01,
      "duration_seconds": 12.58,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.96,
      "end_seconds": 199.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.92,
      "end_seconds": 204.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.06,
      "end_seconds": 205.85,
      "duration_seconds": 0.79,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.28,
      "end_seconds": 237.36,
      "duration_seconds": 18.08,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Okay, so my impression from what you've said is this: This looks most like an asthma flare-up. The reason I say that is that the way you describe it fits together. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had wheezing for three days, and no leg swelling or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.9,
      "end_seconds": 240.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.76,
      "end_seconds": 245.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.63,
      "end_seconds": 246.42,
      "duration_seconds": 0.79,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.24,
      "end_seconds": 283.9,
      "duration_seconds": 24.66,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Let's get a peak flow reading, for asthma control. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'd like you to take prednisolone, 30 milligrams, once a day, for five days. That's for asthma flare-up. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Rinse your mouth after the steroid inhaler."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.86,
      "end_seconds": 298.44,
      "duration_seconds": 13.58,
      "text": "Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. Keep an eye out, and if the inhaler isn't helping or you can't speak in full sentences, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.87,
      "end_seconds": 301.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.18,
      "end_seconds": 310.75,
      "duration_seconds": 8.57,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in two weeks. Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.08,
      "end_seconds": 320.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.46,
      "text": "So, I take the prednisolone, 30 milligrams, once a day and come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.09,
      "end_seconds": 325.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Okay, we're done for today. Take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.39,
      "end_seconds": 329.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "That's everything I wanted to ask. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.05,
      "end_seconds": 330.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}